# A new chat's mode (desktop parity slice 6, Boss 2026-10-28): a row under "on" and "with" that says what each mode means;
# it only sets how the thread is made. The fictional chat fixture runs production OmaChatScreen, with two computers;
# nothing is sent and nothing is answered. Prerequisite: -PartifactPreview :artifact-preview:assembleDebug installed (its newChat extra opens a new chat).
fold folded
rotate portrait
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --ez newChat true
wait 2500
expect on
expect auto · acts without asking
# Look: under "on [Mac Pro]" and "with [Claude]", "runs [auto · acts without asking]", the same small grey word and accent bracket.
shot cover-mode-row
tap auto · acts without asking
expect Claude runs
expect manual · asks before each action
# Look: the menu over the chat, titled "Claude runs", the two modes, each saying what it does.
shot cover-mode-menu
tap manual · asks before each action
expect manual · asks before each action
absent Claude runs
# Look: the row now says "[manual · asks before each action]".
shot cover-mode-manual
key BACK
fold open
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --ez newChat true
wait 2500
expect auto · acts without asking
# Look: the three rows centred under the chat's welcome, the mode row last.
shot unfolded-mode-row
tap auto · acts without asking
tap manual · asks before each action
expect manual · asks before each action
shot unfolded-mode-manual
key BACK
[phone] In Soma chat on the Fold, a new chat shows "runs [auto · acts without asking]"; picking manual and sending makes the thread on the Mac in manual (its first request comes as a card); no card is answered by anything but his tap
